,"roe":10.6,"roa":4.2,"moat":null,"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"analysisUnavailable"},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-03-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:53:24.727Z","evidenceHash":"be9f91481aac7ad23a579ac46cca34cf466444d007dae627456401e80124420c"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-03-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"highRisk","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:53:24.727Z","evidenceHash":"be9f91481aac7ad23a579ac46cca34cf466444d007dae627456401e80124420c"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/MOD.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/MOD.png","website":"https://www.modine.com","ceo":"Neil D. Brinker","full_time_employees":"13200","description":"Modine Manufacturing Company specializes in delivering advanced thermal management systems and heat exchange components, primarily catering to original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) in both on- and off-highway vehicular markets. The company's operations are structured into two main segments: Climate Solutions and Performance Technologies. Its extensive product portfolio encompasses a wide array of heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) solutions. This includes various heating units such as gas-fired, hydronic, electric, and oil-fired models, alongside indoor and outdoor duct furnaces, infrared units, and perimeter heating offerings like commercial fin-tube radiation, cabinet unit heaters, and convectors. Modine also supplies roof-mounted direct- and indirect-fired makeup air units, unit ventilators, single packaged vertical units, and precision air conditioning systems designed for data centers. Further HVAC offerings feature air handler units, fan walls, chillers, ceiling cassettes, hybrid fan coils, and diverse condensers and condensing units. Beyond HVAC, Modine manufactures a range of coils, including microchannel, heat recovery, round tube plate fin, and specialized motor and generator cooling coils. Its comprehensive cooling product line also features evaporator units, fluid coolers, transformer oil coolers, gas and air blast coolers, dry and brine coolers, and remote condensers. Additionally, the company provides protective coatings to guard against corrosion. Furthermore, Modine is a key supplier of advanced thermal management solutions for vehicles. This covers powertrain cooling products such as engine cooling modules, radiators, charge air coolers, condensers, oil coolers, fan shrouds, and surge tanks. On-engine cooling components comprise exhaust gas recirculation (EGR), engine oil, fuel, charge air, and intake air coolers. Auxiliary cooling solutions include transmission and retarder oil coolers, and power steering coolers. The company also offers complete battery thermal management systems and electronics cooling packages, crucial for modern electric and hybrid vehicles. Modine caters to a broad customer base, including original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) in the HVAC, automotive, truck, bus, specialty vehicle, agricultural, industrial, and construction sectors. Its reach extends to construction architects, contractors, and wholesalers of heating equipment, as well as OEMs for commercial and industrial machinery. With a significant global footprint, Modine operates across North America, South America, Europe, and Asia. Established in 1916, Modine Manufacturing Company maintains its corporate headquarters in Racine, Wisconsin.","description_en":"Modine Manufacturing Company specializes in delivering advanced thermal management systems and heat exchange components, primarily catering to original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) in both on- and off-highway vehicular markets. The company's operations are structured into two main segments: Climate Solutions and Performance Technologies. Its extensive product portfolio encompasses a wide array of heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) solutions. This includes various heating units such as gas-fired, hydronic, electric, and oil-fired models, alongside indoor and outdoor duct furnaces, infrared units, and perimeter heating offerings like commercial fin-tube radiation, cabinet unit heaters, and convectors. Modine also supplies roof-mounted direct- and indirect-fired makeup air units, unit ventilators, single packaged vertical units, and precision air conditioning systems designed for data centers. Further HVAC offerings feature air handler units, fan walls, chillers, ceiling cassettes, hybrid fan coils, and diverse condensers and condensing units. Beyond HVAC, Modine manufactures a range of coils, including microchannel, heat recovery, round tube plate fin, and specialized motor and generator cooling coils. Its comprehensive cooling product line also features evaporator units, fluid coolers, transformer oil coolers, gas and air blast coolers, dry and brine coolers, and remote condensers. Additionally, the company provides protective coatings to guard against corrosion. Furthermore, Modine is a key supplier of advanced thermal management solutions for vehicles. This covers powertrain cooling products such as engine cooling modules, radiators, charge air coolers, condensers, oil coolers, fan shrouds, and surge tanks. On-engine cooling components comprise exhaust gas recirculation (EGR), engine oil, fuel, charge air, and intake air coolers. Auxiliary cooling solutions include transmission and retarder oil coolers, and power steering coolers. The company also offers complete battery thermal management systems and electronics cooling packages, crucial for modern electric and hybrid vehicles. Modine caters to a broad customer base, including original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) in the HVAC, automotive, truck, bus, specialty vehicle, agricultural, industrial, and construction sectors. Its reach extends to construction architects, contractors, and wholesalers of heating equipment, as well as OEMs for commercial and industrial machinery. With a significant global footprint, Modine operates across North America, South America, Europe, and Asia. Established in 1916, Modine Manufacturing Company maintains its corporate headquarters in Racine, Wisconsin.","description_zh":"Modine Manufacturing Company（美股代碼：MOD）為 Industrials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Industrial - Machinery 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"1500 DeKoven Avenue","city":"Racine","state":"WI","zip":"53403-2552","country":"US","phone":"262 636 1200","full_address":"1500 DeKoven Avenue, Racine, WI 53403-2552, US","range_52w":"87.84-323.25","year_high":323.25,"year_low":87.84,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":87.84,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-11-04","name":"Mahan Michael Bernard","title":"officer: President, Data Centers","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":328,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-08","name":"Mahan Michael Bernard","title":"officer: President, Commercial HVAC","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":915,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"MODINE MANUFACTURING CO","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":53197549,"price":0,"total_val":0.05},{"date":"2026-09-29","name":"Patten Jeremy Michael","title":"officer: President, Perf. Technologies","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":631,"price":198.07,"total_val":0.12},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Agen Brian Jon","title":"officer: VP, CHRO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":1988,"price":12.28,"total_val":0.02},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Agen Brian Jon","title":"officer: VP, CHRO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":928,"price":17.79,"total_val":0.02},{"date":"2026-09-14","name":"Agen Brian Jon","title":"officer: VP, CHRO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Ex